    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "The previous prediction (rigid subspace → flat/decreasing N_c(w)) was contradicted by the hypothesis (bifurcation → non-monotonic transition) and the surprise metric (1.0). This indicates a need to re-evaluate the constraint construction and verify if the solution space indeed transitions from rigid to disconnected manifold. I will design a numerical experiment to: (1) construct a low-dimensional linear constraint family (rigid case) and a higher-dimensional non-linear constraint family (flexible case), (2) train small feedforward networks using scipy.optimize.minimize(method='L-BFGS-B') to find the minimum width N_c(w) for zero violation (max abs error ≤ 1e-3 on held-out constraints), (3) perform width scans with multiple random seeds to ensure robustness, (4) analyze the trend of N_c(w) vs w to test the bifurcation hypothesis. This approach follows the \"exploration\" mode to search the design space for optimal parameters and validate the hypothesis through empirical evidence."
    },
